Add the retainSnapshot parameter of the snapshot volume policy action, for storages such as Ceph RBD that need the base volume snapshot kept for incremental backups by the block data mover. Velero records the retained snapshot on the DataUpload and deletes it when the backup is deleted, after the repository data and the DataUploads, in a dedicated retained-snapshot controller; snapshots whose deletion persistently fails are escalated to an orphan-snapshot ConfigMap. The parameter names of the snapshot action are validated against a closed list (dataMover, snapshotClass, retainSnapshot), a typo now fails validation instead of silently reading as false. Pre-rollback backups that kept their snapshot through a Retain VolumeSnapshotClass are recovered from the cbt-change-id tag of the repository snapshot.
